*> Implementation test (002-lane-p49n; 18 section 9.4 and 20 sections 7.1, 8.1): a viewer who starts to track a mob is sent the flags that are not at the client's defaults: a climbing
*> spider (metadata 16 BYTE 1) and a mob at its defaults sends nothing extra.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-P49N-VIEW.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY P49NSTATE.
 01 WS-PLAYER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CONN                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DIM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-SPIDER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NEEDED              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CASE                PIC X(100).
 01 WS-CASE240             PIC X(240).
 01 WS-EXP                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-OBS                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-WANTED              BINARY-LONG VALUE 101.
 01 WS-EXPECTED            PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-HEX                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-AREA512             PIC X(512).
 01 WS-ONE                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-IDS                 PIC X(1024).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "MS-TEST-OPEN" USING WS-PLAYER
     MOVE PL-CONN(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-CONN
     MOVE PL-DIM(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-DIM
     COMPUTE WS-X = PL-X(WS-PLAYER) + 3
     MOVE PL-Y(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Y
     MOVE PL-Z(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Z
     MOVE "minecraft:spider" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "PN-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-KEY WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-SPIDER
     CALL "STDMOB-FLAGS-NEEDED" USING WS-SPIDER WS-NEEDED
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§7.1 A spider at its defaults needs no flags packet" TO WS-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-EXP
     MOVE WS-NEEDED TO WS-OBS
     CALL "TEST-CHK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXP WS-OBS
     CALL "PN-ROW-OPEN" USING WS-SPIDER
     MOVE 1 TO PN-CLIMB(WS-SPIDER)
     CALL "STDMOB-FLAGS-NEEDED" USING WS-SPIDER WS-NEEDED
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§7.1 A climbing spider needs it" TO WS-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-EXP
     MOVE WS-NEEDED TO WS-OBS
     CALL "TEST-CHK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXP WS-OBS
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN-IDS" USING WS-CONN WS-IDS
     CALL "ENTITY-VIEWER-FORGET" USING WS-PLAYER
     CALL "ENTITY-VIEWER-REFRESH" USING WS-PLAYER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-AREA512
     MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(EN-ID(WS-SPIDER) + 1) TO WS-AREA512(1:1)
     CALL "TEST-HEX-OF" USING WS-AREA512 WS-ONE WS-HEX
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-EXPECTED
     STRING WS-HEX(1:2) "100001ff" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-EXPECTED
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§7.1 A new viewer of a climbing spider is sent metadata 16 BYTE 1" TO WS-CASE240
     CALL "PN-CHECK-HEX" USING WS-CONN WS-CASE240 WS-WANTED WS-EXPECTED
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-P49N-VIEW.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
